# UI state — ladder, XState, pending/optimistic (always on)

**Golden sentence:** Server/URL state rides loaders and the URL; **everything else** in client UI — including single booleans, menus, `busy`, `open`, `mode` — lives in an **XState v5** actor. Mutating UI never waits silently: paint the **impending** state and prefer **optimistic** success until the server confirms.

## State ladder (use highest row that fits)

| Need | Use | Not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Server / registry / files | Worker handler + `GET /api/*` | Client `useEffect` fetch on mount |
| Route / project / path / open-set flags | **URL** search params or path (+ machine `URL_SYNCED`) | Hidden Handle-only source of truth |
| Loader data per navigation | **Client route loader** (Kody `RouteLoader`) | Duplicate fetch in component |
| Pending submit / optimistic (route forms) | Navigation / form submission state (Remix 3) | Manual `busy` boolean beside Remix |
| **All other client UI state** (toggles, menus, modes, busy, streaming, panel mount, multi-surface) | **XState v5** machine + connector | Handle `let open = false` / `let busy = true` / coordinating booleans |
| Handle role | Subscribe to actor → `handle.update()`; `queueTask` only for one-shot glue when no machine yet | Own product state in closure vars |

## XState always (no "machine tax" carve-out)

Every product UI state in Studio — including Nav/AI rail toggles, menus, `busy`, `open`, `mode`, and panel mount lifecycle — lives in an XState actor. Handle closure vars are **render scratch only**.

| Include | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| Toggles / open flags | rail accordion, menu open, drawer, inspect on/off |
| Modes | chat composer mode, viewport, editor surface, color mode |
| Busy / pending / streaming | panel refresh, SSE turn, save, upload |
| Multi-surface graphs | canvas tabs ↔ DeskPane ↔ URL; shell compact ↔ drawer |
| Async graphs | project load, file open/save, chat sessions hydrate |
| Mount lifecycle | trees portal, media/calendar/workflows bind keys |

**Not product state (exceptions):**

| OK outside machine | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Shareable open-set / route / path | **URL** is source of truth — machine emits/consumes `URL_SYNCED`; never Handle-only flags for shareable state |
| `*-pure.ts` projections | Deterministic transforms — machine orchestrates, pure computes |
| Persistence adapters | `*-store.ts` (localStorage) — machine invokes via connector actors |
| True DOM-only scratch | Timer ids, ResizeObserver refs, one-frame focus ring with no chrome effect |

**Forbidden:** `let fooOpen = false` / `let busy = true` / ad-hoc mode enums as the owner of product UI. If UI can desync, race, or be tested as a graph — it is a machine.

### Shape

```
*-machine.ts       # pure createMachine — no DOM/fetch
*-machine.test.ts  # actor + events → context / snapshot
*-connector.ts     # .provide() I/O (DeskPane, localStorage, URL, fetch)
*-api.ts           # deep public interface for hosts / plugins (optional)
```

Host imports **connector** (or API facade) only — never the raw machine from UI trees. UI projects `actor.getSnapshot()` (or connector `getState()`) then `handle.update()`. Plugins customize by **providing** machine actions/actors — not by forking `app.tsx`.

```typescript
export function StudioRoute(handle: Handle) {
  const filesActor = createFilesPanelConnector({ /* deps */ })
  filesActor.subscribe(() => handle.update())
  return () => {
    const { files, status } = filesActor.getSnapshot().context
    const loading = status === "loading"
    return (/* JSX using files, loading */)
  }
}
```

Side-effects live in machine connectors / loaders — not in pure modules. Do **not** park `loading` as a Handle `let`.

## Pending + optimistic

**Golden sentence:** Mutating UI never waits silently on the network — paint the **impending** (in-flight) state, and prefer **optimistic** success from intent/`formData` until the server confirms or rejects.

| UX | Do | Don't |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Pending / impending** | Show in-flight chrome (disabled control, frame fallback, machine `pending`/`submitting`) on every mutating action | Fire-and-forget with no visual change until response |
| **Optimistic** | Default — render future state from submission intent / `formData` / machine context; rollback on failure | Manual `busy` boolean + blank wait as the only feedback |
| **Pending-only OK** | No safe future state yet (upload %, unknown result shape) — still show progress / disabled | Spinner with no ownership of which action is in flight |

Failed action → revert optimistic paint (error boundary, loader revalidation, or machine error transition). Never leave a lied-about success.

### Who owns it

| Surface | Owner | Not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Forms, route navigations, frame loads | **Remix 3** — navigation / form submission state, frame pending fallbacks, `FormData` as optimistic source | Ad-hoc `let busy = true` clusters |
| All Studio chrome UI (toggles, menus, panels, wizards, multi-surface) | **XState** — context holds **intent + pending** (and open/mode); connector does I/O | Separate `isSaving` / `*Open` flags beside or instead of the machine |
| True DOM-only focus ring | Handle closure scratch OK | Owning menu/drawer/busy in Handle |

XState does **not** replace Remix for simple route form submits. For every other graph, impending/optimistic live in that machine's context — don't bolt a second busy layer on the host.

## Agent checklist (every UI edit)

- [ ] New UI state → `*-machine.ts` (+ test) + connector; not a Handle `let`
- [ ] No new `busy` / `*Open` / mode owned only in `app.tsx` or a host closure
- [ ] Shareable flags still go through URL + machine sync
- [ ] Host reads snapshot / connector API — does not mirror machine fields into parallel Handle lets
- [ ] Every new mutating control has impending UI (and optimistic when a safe future state exists)
- [ ] Rollback path exists (revalidate, error transition, or restore snapshot)

